England is almost certain to qualify for the 2016 European Championship. However, the manager Roy Hodgson still does not know which best team to pick.

Sports newspaper reporters have picked their starting teams for the final games in France. They assume all the players are fit to play. Please tell us your choice of England's starting team by posting it in the comments section below.

Roy Hodgson was pictured at the Juventus Stadium during a friendly game against Italy on Tuesday. The suggested team is:

Goalkeeper: Hart;
Defenders: Clyne, Cahill, Jagielka, Baines;
Midfield: Henderson, Wilshere;
For forward: Welbeck, Rooney, Sterling;
Striker: Kane.
